Stage 1 has no separate rule-first proof phase: `prove.sh` compiles `verification.k` with all four rules present and proves only the target claim, while the other `kprove` runs are negative mutation probes. Therefore none qualifies as `PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA`. Each canonical rule is an equation for one of the three proof-local total summary functions, so all four classify as `DEFINITION`; there are no operational rules or domain lemmas in the canonical local closure.
Mounted evidence confirms the inventory has four proof-local summary equations and no separately proved rule, operational rule, simplification rule, or additional mathematical lemma.
